      "math_academy_id": "q-161678",
      "sequence_position": 13,
      "problem": "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the $xy$-plane, the surface $z={e}^{x+y},$ and the planes $x=0,$ $x=1,$ $y=0,$ $y=1.$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that our solid can be written as a type I region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le {e}^{x+y}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{e}^{x+y}}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[z]_{z=0}^{z={e}^{x+y}}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x+y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{e}^{x+y}]_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x+1}-{e}^{x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[{e}^{x+1}-{e}^{x}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =({e}^{1+1}-{e}^{1})-({e}^{0+1}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{2}-e-e+1 \\\\  & =(e-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
      "result": "Correct",
      "grade": "Correct",
